verses.tf_en:
① **«قَالَ ذٰلِكَ بَیْنِیْ وَبَیْنَكَ»** (Musa said: “That is agreed between me and you.”) — Sayyiduna Musa gracefully accepted the marital proposal and ratified the bilateral agreement;
② **«اَیَّمَا الْاَجَلَیْنِ قَضَیْتُ فَلَا عُدْوَانَ عَلَیَّ»** (“Whichever of the two terms I fulfil, there shall be no grievance or demand against me...”) — Whether he completed the obligatory eight years or the voluntary ten years, the marital contract would be fully discharged without any additional claim or reproach.
③ **«وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰی مَا نَقُوْلُ وَكِیْلٌ»** (“...and Allah is the Guardian and Witness over what we say.”) — Solemnly invoking Allah Almighty as the supreme Trustee, Overseer, and Guarantor of their sacred pact. (The authentic Hadith confirms that Sayyiduna Musa, embodying supreme prophetic generosity, fulfilled the more generous and complete term of ten years).

① **«فَلَمَّا قَضٰی مُوْسَی الْاَجَلَ وَسَارَ بِاَهْلِهٖۤ»** (So when Musa had completed the term and was travelling with his family) — Having completed the full ten-year covenant in Madyan, Sayyiduna Musa took leave of his father-in-law and set forth with his blessed wife (Safura) and flock towards his homeland of Egypt;
② **«اٰنَسَ مِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ نَارًا»** (He perceived a fire from the direction of Mount Tur.) — On an intensely pitch-dark, freezing night in the wilderness of Sinai, during which his wife went into labor and his flint refused to spark, Musa suddenly caught sight of a luminous fire glowing serenely on the slopes of the sacred mountain;
③ **«قَالَ لِاَهْلِهِ امْكُثُوْۤا اِنِّیْۤ اٰنَسْتُ نَارًا»** (He said to his household: “Stay here; indeed, I perceive a fire...”) — He instructed his family to remain sheltered while he went forward alone to investigate the radiant blaze;
④ **«لَّعَلِّیْۤ اٰتِیْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ»** (“...perhaps I may bring you from there some information...”) — Hoping to meet travellers who could direct them to the correct path out of the desert;
⑤ **«اَوْ جَذْوَةٍ مِّنَ النَّارِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُوْنَ»** (“...or a flaming brand from the fire so that you may warm yourselves.”) — Or retrieve a burning branch to kindle their hearth and provide warmth against the piercing winter chill. What he anticipated as earthly fire was in reality the uncreated manifest Nur of the Divine Majesty!

① **«وَاَنْ اَلْقِ عَصَاكَ»** (“And cast down your staff!”) — The Divine Command directed him to cast to the earth the wooden shepherd’s staff in his hand;
② **«فَلَمَّا رَاٰهَا تَهْتَزُّ كَاَنَّهَا جَاۤنٌّ»** (So when he saw it writhing as though it were a swift, terrifying serpent) — Instantly upon touching the ground, the inert wood was miraculously transmuted into a massive, fearsome dragon or serpent moving with lightning agility;
③ **«وَّلّٰی مُدْبِرًا وَّلَمْ یُعَقِّبْ»** (he turned away fleeing and did not look back.) — Overwhelmed by natural human awe and dread at this sudden colossal prodigy, Sayyiduna Musa retreated swiftly without turning around;
④ **«یَا مُوسَىٰ أَقْبِلْ وَلَا تَخَفْ»** (“O Musa! Come forward and do not fear!”) — The Lord of the Worlds called out to him with sovereign reassurance, commanding him to return and take hold of the creature;
⑤ **«اِنَّكَ مِنَ الْاٰمِنِیْنَ»** (“Indeed, you are of those who are entirely secure.”) — Confirming that in the divine presence, His chosen Messengers are completely safeguarded against all danger, dread, and harm.

① **«اُسْلُكْ یَدَكَ فِیْ جَیْبِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَیْضَاۤءَ مِنْ غَیْرِ سُوْۤءٍ»** (“Insert your hand into the opening of your robe; it will come out shining white without any blemish!”) — Musa was commanded to place his right hand into his collar, and upon withdrawing it, it shone with a dazzling, brilliant light like the radiant sun or a celestial beacon, completely devoid of vitiligo, leprosy, or any defect. This was the celebrated miracle of the Radiant Hand (*Yad al-Bayda'*);
② **«وَّاضْمُمْ اِلَیْكَ جَنَاحَكَ مِنَ الرَّهْبِ»** (“And draw your arm close to your chest to dispel all fear!”) — Whenever struck by natural awe or dread before Pharaoh or supernatural manifestations, he was instructed to place his hand over his heart, which would instantly dissolve all fear and envelop his soul in serene fortitude;
③ **«فَذٰنِكَ بُرْهَانٰنِ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ اِلٰی فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَائِهٖ»** (“These are two conclusive proofs from your Lord to Pharaoh and his chiefs;”) — The miraculous Staff and the Radiant Hand were the two paramount undeniable celestial signs commissioned to challenge the haughty court of Egypt;
④ **«اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِیْنَ»** (“...indeed, they are a defiantly rebellious people.”) — Transgressors who had forsaken faith, enslaved humanity, and defiantly defied the sovereignty of Allah.

① **«قَالَ سَنَشُدُّ عَضُدَكَ بِاَخِیْكَ»** (He said: “We will soon strengthen your arm with your brother...”) — Allah Almighty graciously granted Musa’s noble supplication, commissioning Sayyiduna Harun with prophethood and binding them together as an invincible fraternity of truth;
② **«وَنَجْعَلُ لَكُمَا سُلْطٰنًا فَلَا یَصِلُوْنَ اِلَیْكُمَا»** (“...and We will bestow upon both of you clear authority and dominance, so they will not be able to harm you;”) — Granting them an aura of divine majesty (*haybah*) and miraculous prestige that would paralyze the executioners, rendering the royal guards powerless to lay a hand upon them;
③ **«بِاٰیٰتِنَاۤ اَنْتُمَا وَمَنِ اتَّبَعَكُمَا الْغٰلِبُوْنَ»** (“...by virtue of Our Signs; you two and those who follow you shall be the triumphant!”) — Issuing an unconditional celestial decree: backed by the irresistible miracles of Allah, the two prophetic brothers and all sincere believers who rally behind them are guaranteed ultimate victory over the forces of tyranny.

① **«فَلَمَّا جَاۤءَهُمْ مُّوْسٰی بِاٰیٰتِنَا بَیِّنٰتٍ»** (So when Musa came to them with Our clear, manifest Signs) — Entering Pharaoh’s throne room accompanied by Harun, Sayyiduna Musa proclaimed monotheism and manifested the miraculous Staff and Radiant Hand before the entire assembly of imperial dignitaries;
② **«قَالُوْا مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّفْتَرًی»** (they said: “This is nothing but fabricated magic...”) — Incapable of rational rebuttal and blinded by arrogance, the courtiers dismissed the divine miracles as fraudulent sorcery and optical trickery;
③ **«وَّمَا سَمِعْنَا بِهٰذَا فِیْۤ اٰبَاۤئِنَا الْاَوَّلِیْنَ»** (“...and we never heard of anything like this among our ancient forefathers!”) — Clinging blindly to the pagan polytheism of their ancestors, they absurdly argued that because pure monotheism was unfamiliar to their lineage, it had to be rejected.

① **«وَقَالَ مُوْسٰی رَبِّیْۤ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ جَاۤءَ بِالْهُدٰی مِنْ عِنْدِهٖ»** (And Musa said: “My Lord knows best who has brought guidance from Him...”) — Rebuffing their mockery with serene prophetic dignity, he affirmed that Allah alone is the all-knowing witness over genuine revelation and apostolic truth;
② **«وَمَنْ تَكُوْنُ لَهٗ عَاقِبَةُ الدَّارِ»** (“...and for whom will be the ultimate good end in the Abode of the Hereafter;”) — The final, everlasting victory and eternal paradise belong solely to the righteous believers, not to worldly despots;
③ **«اِنَّهٗ لَا یُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ»** (“...surely the wrongdoers shall never prosper!”) — Declaring an immutable divine law: all oppressors, idolaters, and tyrants are destined for ruin, both in the trials of this world and in the fires of the next.

① **«وَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ یَا أَیُّهَا الْمَلَأُ مَا عَلِمْتُ لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَیْرِی»** (And Pharaoh proclaimed: “O council! I know of no god for you other than myself!”) — Reaching the zenith of demonic haughtiness, Pharaoh asserted absolute personal divinity before his subservient subjects;
② **«فَأَوْقِدْ لِی یَا هَامَانُ عَلَى الطِّینِ»** (“So kindle a fire for me, O Haman, upon the clay...”) — He ordered his grand vizier and chief architect Haman to manufacture baked ceramic bricks, marking an early historical reference to mass kiln-fired brick construction in Egypt;
③ **«فَاجْعَلْ لِّیْ صَرْحًا لَّعَلِّیْۤ اَطَّلِعُ اِلٰۤی اِلٰهِ مُوْسٰی»** (“...and erect for me a towering, lofty monument so that I may look upon the God of Musa;”) — In his crude anthropomorphic foolishness, he imagined that the Lord of Creation occupied a physical spatial location in the clouds that could be reached by an earthly tower;
④ **«وَاِنِّیْ لَاَظُنُّهٗ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِیْنَ»** (“...and indeed, I certainly think he is of the liars!”) — Blasphemously asserting that Musa’s claim of an unseen Lord who transcends the physical universe was an outright fabrication.

① **«وَلَقَدْ اٰتَیْنَا مُوْسَی الْكِتٰبَ»** (And We certainly gave Musa the Scripture...) — Following the drowning of Pharaoh, Allah revealed the original Torah inscribed on tablets upon Mount Tur to Sayyiduna Musa;
② **«مِنْ بَعْدِ مَاۤ اَهْلَكْنَا الْقُرُوْنَ الْاُوْلٰی»** (“...after We had destroyed the earlier generations,”) — Sadrul Afazil highlights that after the destruction of the earlier nations (the peoples of Nuh, 'Ad, Thamud, and Pharaoh), Allah ceased annihilating entire nations by wholesale natural cataclysms, instituting instead sacred law, guidance, and righteous struggle through divine scripture;
③ **«بَصَاۤئِرَ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدًی وَّرَحْمَةً»** (as enlightenment for the eyes of the hearts of mankind, a guidance, and a mercy,) — Illumination enabling souls to distinguish between truth and falsehood, providing detailed ethical statutes and boundless divine mercy;
④ **«لَّعَلَّهُمْ یَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ»** (so that they might take heed and be reminded.) — Reflecting on the divine commandments and striving for eternal salvation.

① **«وَمَا كُنْتَ بِجَانِبِ الْغَرْبِیِّ»** (And you were not on the western side of the Mount...) — Addressing His Beloved, the Master of Creation Sayyiduna Muhammad Mustafa ﷺ: You were not physically present on the western slope of Mount Sinai;
② **«اِذْ قَضَیْنَاۤ اِلٰی مُوْسَی الْاَمْرَ»** (when We decreed the commandment of Prophethood and the Law to Musa,) — When Allah appointed Musa as Messenger, spoke to him directly, and bestowed upon him the sacred tablets;
③ **«وَمَا كُنْتَ مِنَ الشّٰهِدِیْنَ»** (nor were you among the eyewitnesses.) — Classical Sunni scholars, including Imam Ahmad Raza Khan, emphasize that this verse establishes the supreme miracle of the Prophet’s bestowed knowledge of the unseen (*'Ilm al-Ghayb al-'Ata'i*): having never physically witnessed these ancient events nor studied under earthly scholars, his effortless, flawless, and vivid narration of these historical episodes to the Jewish and Christian rabbis is decisive scriptural proof that his knowledge is directly unveiled by Allah Almighty through divine revelation!

① **«وَلٰكِنَّاۤ اَنْشَاْنَا قُرُوْنًا فَتَطَاوَلَ عَلَیْهِمُ الْعُمُرُ»** (But We brought forth many generations, and long ages passed over them;) — In the long centuries between Musa and the advent of the Final Prophet ﷺ, nations drifted away from prophetic guidance, scripture was corrupted, and primordial truth was obscured;
② **«وَمَا كُنْتَ ثَاوِیًا فِیْۤ اَهْلِ مَدْیَنَ تَتْلُوْا عَلَیْهِمْ اٰیٰتِنَا»** (and you were not a resident dwelling among the people of Madyan, reciting Our Signs to them;) — You never resided in the desert of Madyan to witness Musa watering the flock or marrying the daughter of Shu'ayb;
③ **«وَلٰكِنَّا كُنَّا مُرْسِلِیْنَ»** (but it is We Who sent Messengers and revealed these matters to you.) — Allah chose you as the Seal of all Messengers and enriched your blessed soul with the treasures of unseen historical gnosis.

① **«وَمَا كُنْتَ بِجَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ اِذْ نَادَیْنَا»** (And nor were you beside Mount Tur when We called out;) — You were not standing on the slopes of Sinai when Allah addressed Musa from the blessed tree;
② **«وَلٰكِنْ رَّحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ»** (but this revelation is a supreme mercy from your Lord,) — Imparting this celestial knowledge to you is a specialized mercy and cosmic honour;
③ **«لِتُنذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّا أَتَاهُم مِّن نَّذِیرٍ مِّن قَبْلِكَ»** (so that you may warn a people to whom no warner came before you,) — Specifically the Arabs of the Hijaz, who had endured an extended era of prophetic cessation (*Fatrah*) since the times of Isma'il;
④ **«لَعَلَّهُمْ یَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ»** (in order that they may reflect and take heed.) — Awakening them from the stupor of idolatry to embrace the light of pure monotheism.

① **«فَلَمَّا جَاۤءَهُمُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ عِنْدِنَا»** (Yet when the Truth came to them from Us...) — When the Holy Prophet ﷺ arrived carrying the miraculous, living Quran,
② **«قَالُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُوْتِیَ مِثْلَ مَاۤ اُوْتِیَ مُوْسٰی»** (they obstinately demanded: “Why was he not given the like of what was given to Musa?”) — Demanding physical prodigies like the parting of the sea or a scripture written in full on tablets at one single time;
③ **«اَوَلَمْ یَكْفُرُوْا بِمَاۤ اُوْتِیَ مُوْسٰی مِنْ قَبْلُ»** (Did they not already disbelieve in what was given to Musa before?) — Exposing their hypocrisy: even when such physical miracles were manifested to their predecessors, did they not obstinately reject Musa as well?
④ **«قَالُوْا سِحْرٰنِ تَظٰهَرَا»** (They said: “Two works of magic supporting each other!”) — Disparaging both the Torah and the Quran, or Musa and Muhammad ﷺ, as twin sorcerers mutually validating each other;
⑤ **«وَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا بِكُلٍّ كٰفِرُوْنَ»** (and they proclaimed: “Indeed, we disbelieve in all of them!”) — Unmasking their deep-seated defiance against all divine revelation regardless of form.

① **«فَاِنْ لَّمْ یَسْتَجِیْبُوْا لَكَ»** (So if they fail to respond to your challenge,) — If they cannot produce such a book—and they never can;
② **«فَاعْلَمْ اَنَّمَا یَتَّبِعُوْنَ اَهْوَاۤءَهُمْ»** (then know with certainty that they merely follow their own base desires;) — Their denial stems not from logical inquiry, but from pride, stubborn tribalism, and carnal whims (*hawa*);
③ **«وَمَنْ أَضَلُّ مِمَّنِ اتَّبَعَ هَوَاهُ بِغَیْرِ هُدًى مِّنَ اللَّهِ»** (And who is more astray than one who follows his desires without any guidance from Allah?) — There exists no soul more profoundly misguided than one who abandons divine light to worship the idol of personal desire;
④ **«اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا یَهْدِی الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِیْنَ»** (Indeed, Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.) — Depriving hardened oppressors of divine grace (*Tawfiq*) because of their deliberate choice of falsehood over truth.

① **«وَاِذَا یُتْلٰی عَلَیْهِمْ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِهٖۤ»** (And when it is recited to them, they declare: “We believe in it;”) — With tears streaming down their faces in profound spiritual ecstasy upon hearing the recitation of the Quran, they bear witness to its celestial truth;
② **«اِنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّنَاۤ»** (“indeed, it is the absolute Truth from our Lord;”) — Acknowledging that its eloquence, coherence, and sublime wisdom could only emanate from the Creator;
③ **«اِنَّا كُنَّا مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ مُسْلِمِیْنَ»** (“surely even before this we were Muslims, surrendered in faith!”) — Adhering to the original, uncorrupted monotheistic teachings of Musa and 'Isa, they were already spiritually surrendered to Allah, eagerly awaiting the advent of the Promised Prophet ﷺ.

① **«اُولٰۤئِكَ یُؤْتَوْنَ اَجْرَهُمْ مَّرَّتَیْنِ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا»** (These shall be granted their reward twice over because of their patience;) — The Holy Prophet ﷺ affirmed that three categories of people receive a double reward, foremost among them being a believer from the People of the Book who believed in his first Prophet and subsequently believed with patience and fortitude in the Final Prophet ﷺ;
② **«وَیَدْرَءُوْنَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ السَّیِّئَةَ»** (and they repel evil with good,) — Answering insults with gentleness, ignorance with wisdom, and enmity with forgiveness;
③ **«وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ یُنْفِقُوْنَ»** (and spend out of what We have provided them.) — Generously expending their lawful wealth in charitable avenues for the pleasure of Allah.

① **«وَاِذَا سَمِعُوا اللَّغْوَ اَعْرَضُوْا عَنْهُ»** (And when they hear vain or abusive speech, they turn away from it) — Preserving their spiritual purity, they refuse to engage in vulgarity, slander, or hostile polemics initiated by pagan mockers;
② **«وَقَالُوْا لَنَاۤ اَعْمَالُنَا وَلَكُمْ اَعْمَالُكُمْ»** (and say: “For us are our deeds, and for you are your deeds;”) — Expressing calm disavowal of falsehood and personal accountability before God;
③ **«سَلٰمٌ عَلَیْكُمْ لَا نَبْتَغِی الْجٰهِلِیْنَ»** (“Peace be upon you; we seek not the company of the ignorant!”) — A parting formula of peaceful disengagement (*Salam al-Mutaarakah*), exemplifying the noble forbearance of the saints who decline to trade insults with foolish agitators.

① **«اِنَّكَ لَا تَهْدِیْ مَنْ اَحْبَبْتَ»** (Indeed, you cannot guide whomever you love...) — Classical Sunni orthodox creed, elucidated by Imam Fakhruddin ar-Razi and Ala Hazrat Imam Ahmad Raza Khan, draws an essential theological distinction here: The Beloved Prophet ﷺ is indeed the universal guide who points out and expounds the path of truth (*Hidayat al-Irshad wa ad-Dalalah*), as affirmed in *«وَإِنَّكَ لَتَهْدِی إِلَىٰ صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِیمٍ»* (Surah Ash-Shura 42:52). However, creating the light of faith within the heart and bestowing the grace of belief (*Tawfiq al-Iman*) is the exclusive sovereign prerogative of Allah Almighty alone. This verse was revealed regarding the Prophet’s deep compassion for his uncle Abu Talib at the time of his passing, when the Prophet ﷺ implored him to utter the Kalimah, yet divine decree had not written faith for him;
② **«وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ یَهْدِیْ مَنْ یَّشَاۤءُ»** (...but Allah guides whomever He wills;) — Faith is a celestial gift bestowed by divine selection according to eternal divine wisdom;
③ **«وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِیْنَ»** (and He knows best who are the receptive to guidance.) — Allah alone possesses perfect, eternal knowledge of which souls are genuinely worthy and predisposed to receive the light of faith.

① **«وَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ نَّتَّبِعِ الْهُدٰی مَعَكَ نُتَخَطَّفْ مِنْ اَرْضِنَا»** (And they say: “If we follow the guidance with you, we would be snatched away from our land!”) — The pagan Quraysh of Mecca offered a flimsy political excuse for their disbelief, alleging that if they abandoned idol worship and embraced Islam, the surrounding hostile Arab tribes would unite and expel them from Mecca;
② **«اَوَلَمْ نُمَكِّنْ لَّهُمْ حَرَمًا اٰمِنًا»** (Have We not established for them a secure Sanctuary...) — Refuting their groundless fear, Allah reminds them that He made the sacred precinct of Mecca a revered sanctuary (*Haram Amin*) where warfare, bloodshed, and raiding were strictly forbidden, protecting them while the rest of Arabia was plagued by tribal anarchy;
③ **«یُّجْبٰۤی اِلَیْهِ ثَمَرٰتُ كُلِّ شَیْءٍ رِّزْقًا مِّنْ لَّدُنَّا»** (to which are brought the fruits of every kind as a provision from Us?) — In fulfillment of the prayer of Sayyiduna Ibrahim, caravans from across the world transport abundant produce, provisions, and trade goods to their barren valley;
④ **«وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا یَعْلَمُوْنَ»** (Yet most of them do not know.) — They fail to comprehend that the God Who protected them in their infidelity is all the more capable of safeguarding them if they embrace His true religion!

① **«وَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْیَةٍۭ بَطِرَتْ مَعِیْشَتَهَا»** (And how many a city have We destroyed that exulted insolently in its luxuriant livelihood!) — Historical reminder of countless ancient metropolises that grew vain, haughty, and ungrateful in the midst of material extravagance, forgetting their Creator and persecuting the righteous;
② **«فَتِلْكَ مَسٰكِنُهُمْ لَمْ تُسْكَنْ مِّنْ بَعْدِهِمْ اِلَّا قَلِیْلًا»** (So there lie their desolate dwellings, uninhabited after them except for a little while;) — Their once magnificent palaces and vibrant settlements were transformed into ghost towns, occasionally visited only by passing travellers taking brief shelter;
③ **«وَكُنَّا نَحْنُ الْوٰرِثِیْنَ»** (and it is We Who were the ultimate Inheritors!) — All their accumulated gold, mansions, and temporal pomp vanished, while the Ever-Living, Sovereign Lord remains as the sole heir of the heavens and the earth.

① **«وَمَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ مُهْلِكَ الْقُرٰی»** (And your Lord would never destroy any townships...) — Highlighting the absolute divine justice: Allah Almighty does not subject human settlements to wholesale destruction upon sudden whim or arbitrary wrath;
② **«حَتّٰی یَبْعَثَ فِیْۤ اُمِّهَا رَسُوْلًا یَّتْلُوْا عَلَیْهِمْ اٰیٰتِنَا»** (“...until He sends a noble Messenger to their principal mother-city, reciting Our verses to them;”) — Establishing conclusive prophetic proof (*Iqamat al-Hujjah*) by commissioning a Messenger to the metropolis or capital (*Umm al-Qura*, such as Mecca for Arabia and the world), ensuring the divine revelation radiates outwards to all surrounding regions;
③ **«وَمَا كُنَّا مُهْلِكِی الْقُرٰۤی اِلَّا وَاَهْلُهَا ظٰلِمُوْنَ»** (“...and never did We destroy the townships unless their inhabitants were persistent wrongdoers.”) — Divine chastisement is visited only when the populace adamantly rejects the clear apostolic truth, obstinately persists in polytheism, and perpetrates ruthless oppression.

① **«وَمَا أُوتِیتُم مِّن شَیْءٍ فَمَتَاعُ الْحَیَاةِ الدُّنْیَا وَزِینَتُهَا»** (And whatever thing you have been granted is merely a passing provision of worldly life and its transient glitter;) — All accumulated worldly assets—wealth, power, progeny, and physical pleasures—are ephemeral utilities destined to perish with the grave;
② **«وَمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَیْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰی»** (“...and that which is with Allah is vastly superior and more enduring;”) — The spiritual rewards and everlasting bliss of Paradise prepared by Allah are infinitely pure in quality and boundless in duration;
③ **«اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ»** (“...do you not then employ your intellect?”) — Exhorting humanity to use sound discernment: why exchange the permanent, peerless treasures of the Hereafter for the fleeting, trivial illusions of this mortal world?

① **«اَفَمَنْ وَّعَدْنٰهُ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا فَهُوَ لَاقِیْهِ»** (Is he whom We have promised a fair, bountiful promise—which he will certainly attain—...) — Can a sincere believer who strives righteously in this world, relying on Allah’s infallible promise of eternal Paradise and celestial honour;
② **«كَمَن مَّتَّعْنَاهُ مَتَاعَ الْحَیَاةِ الدُّنْیَا»** (...be equal to him whom We have merely granted the fleeting pleasures of this worldly life,...) — Who indulges his carnal passions in disbelief and arrogance;
③ **«ثُمَّ هُوَ یَوْمَ الْقِیٰمَةِ مِنَ الْمُحْضَرِیْنَ»** (...and then on the Day of Resurrection he shall be among those arraigned in chains?) — Brought forward as a humiliated captive to be hurled into the blazing abyss of Jahannam? Reason and justice dictate that the two can never be equated.

① **«قَالَ الَّذِیْنَ حَقَّ عَلَیْهِمُ الْقَوْلُ»** (Those against whom the decree of punishment has been justified will plead:) — The demonic leaders, false priests, and tyrannical chieftains upon whom divine wrath is sealed will attempt to absolve themselves from the guilt of their followers;
② **«رَبَّنَا هٰۤؤُلَاۤءِ الَّذِیْنَ اَغْوَیْنَا اَغْوَیْنٰهُمْ كَمَا غَوَیْنَا»** (“Our Lord! These are the ones whom we led astray; we led them astray only as we ourselves went astray;”) — Acknowledging that while they invited them to misguidance, they had no coercive power over them; the followers had willingly chosen to imitate their disbelief;
③ **«تَبَرَّاْنَاۤ اِلَیْكَ»** (“...we completely disown them before You;”) — Severing all allegiances and friendships in terror before the divine judgment;
④ **«مَا كَانُوْۤا اِیَّانَا یَعْبُدُوْنَ»** (“...it was not us that they worshipped!”) — In reality, they were worshipping their own lusts, devils, and caprices rather than any true authority.

① **«وَقِیْلَ ادْعُوْا شُرَكَاۤءَكُمْ»** (And it will be said to them: “Call upon your ascribed partners!”) — To intensify their humiliation, the polytheists will be commanded to invoke their idols, saints, or deities to rescue them from the impending doom;
② **«فَدَعَوْهُمْ فَلَمْ یَسْتَجِیْبُوْا لَهُمْ»** (So they will call upon them, but they will not respond to them at all;) — The inanimate stones and false gods will remain completely mute and impotent, offering not a whisper of assistance;
③ **«وَرَاَوُا الْعَذَابَ»** (and they shall behold the torment;) — Seeing the roaring inferno of Hell laid bare before their eyes;
④ **«لَوْ اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا یَهْتَدُوْنَ»** (if only they had accepted guidance!) — How bitterly they will lament their wasted earthly lives, wishing they had embraced faith and followed the true Messengers.

① **«وَرَبُّكَ یَخْلُقُ مَا یَشَاۤءُ وَیَخْتَارُ»** (And your Lord creates whatever He wills and chooses;) — Establishing the sovereign omnipotence and absolute autonomy of the Divine Will: Allah alone creates all existence and selects whomsoever He pleases for prophethood, grace, and spiritual distinction without compulsion or obligation;
② **«مَا كَانَ لَهُمُ الْخِیَرَةُ»** (“...it was never for them to have the choice;”) — No created being—neither idolater, king, nor philosopher—possesses any authority to choose or dictate to Allah who should be appointed as a Messenger or what divine law should be promulgated;
③ **«سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ وَتَعٰلٰی عَمَّا یُشْرِكُوْنَ»** (Exalted is Allah and Far Transcendent above whatever partners they ascribe to Him!) — Sanctifying His absolute Oneness (*Tawhid*) from the blasphemous polytheism and flawed human assumptions ascribed to Him.

① **«وَهُوَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ»** (And He is Allah; there is no deity worthy of worship except Him!) — Proclaiming the foundational creed of Islamic monotheism;
② **«لَهُ الْحَمْدُ فِی الْاُوْلٰی وَالْاٰخِرَةِ»** (To Him belongs all praise in the first life and in the Hereafter;) — Praised in this world for His innumerable material and spiritual bounties, and praised in the Hereafter by the dwellers of Paradise for His infinite justice, grace, and mercy;
③ **«وَلَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَاِلَیْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ»** (and His alone is the sovereign command, and unto Him you shall all be returned!) — The ultimate legislative authority and final judicial verdict belong exclusively to Him, and before His tribunal all creation must stand for retribution.

① **«قُلْ أَرَأَیْتُمْ إِن جَعَلَ اللَّهُ عَلَیْكُمُ اللَّیْلَ سَرْمَدًا إِلَىٰ یَوْمِ الْقِیَامَةِ»** (Proclaim: “Have you considered: if Allah were to make the night perpetual over you until the Day of Resurrection...”) — Challenging human intellect with an undeniable cosmic reality: imagine the catastrophe if the earth were plunged into perpetual darkness without a dawn;
② **«مَنْ اِلٰهٌ غَیْرُ اللّٰهِ یَاْتِیْكُمْ بِضِیَاۤءٍ»** (“...who is the deity besides Allah that could bring you light?”) — Could any idol, celestial body, or human technology recreate the life-giving radiance of the sun and sustain earthly existence?
③ **«اَفَلَا تَسْمَعُوْنَ»** (“Do you not then listen?”) — Heeding this profound rational reminder with receptive hearts and submissive faith.

① **«قُلْ اَرَءَیْتُمْ اِنْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلَیْكُمُ النَّهَارَ سَرْمَدًا اِلٰی یَوْمِ الْقِیٰمَةِ»** (Proclaim: “Have you considered: if Allah were to make the day perpetual over you until the Day of Resurrection...”) — Consider the reverse calamity: if the scorching glare of daylight never ceased;
② **«مَنْ اِلٰهٌ غَیْرُ اللّٰهِ یَاْتِیْكُمْ بِلَیْلٍ تَسْكُنُوْنَ فِیْهِ»** (“...who is the deity besides Allah that could bring you night in which you might rest?”) — How could living bodies endure without the restorative tranquility and coolness of darkness?
③ **«اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَ»** (“Do you not then perceive?”) — Beholding the magnificent wisdom embedded in the alternating tapestry of cosmic order.

① **«وَمِن رَّحْمَتِهِ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ اللَّیْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ»** (And out of His mercy He has appointed for you the night and the day:) — Highlighting that the seamless cycle of dawn and dusk is not a mechanical accident, but an intentional manifestation of divine compassion;
② **«لِتَسْكُنُوْا فِیْهِ»** (that you may rest therein during the night,) — Refreshing the mind and rejuvenating the body in quiet repose;
③ **«وَلِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ»** (and that you may seek of His bounty during the day,) — Dispersing across the land to engage in lawful commerce, agriculture, and livelihood;
④ **«وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ»** (and in order that you may be grateful.) — Fulfilling the purpose of creation by recognizing these daily blessings and rendering heartfelt gratitude (*Shukr*) to the Beneficent Creator.

① **«وَنَزَعْنَا مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ شَهِیْدًا»** (And We shall draw out from every nation a witness...) — On Judgment Day, Allah will summon the Prophet of each generation as the authoritative celestial witness (*shahid*) over the deeds and faith of his community (with the Holy Prophet Muhammad ﷺ presiding as the supreme witness over all Prophets and nations);
② **«فَقُلْنَا هَاتُوْا بُرْهَانَكُمْ»** (...and We shall say to the deniers: “Produce your conclusive proof!”) — Demanding that polytheists present any legitimate scriptural or rational evidence to substantiate their idolatry;
③ **«فَعَلِمُوْۤا اَنَّ الْحَقَّ لِلّٰهِ»** (Then they will realize that the absolute Truth belongs exclusively to Allah,) — Confronted by the testimony of their Prophets and the majesty of God, all doubts will evaporate and the undeniable sovereignty of Allah will be manifest;
④ **«وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا یَفْتَرُوْنَ»** (and all that they used to invent will vanish from them!) — Every idol, intercessory fantasy, and false myth will dissolve into nothingness.

① **«اِنَّ قَارُوْنَ كَانَ مِنْ قَوْمِ مُوْسٰی فَبَغٰی عَلَیْهِمْ»** (Indeed, Qarun was from the people of Musa, but he tyrannized over them;) — The historical narrative shifts to the infamous tycoon Qarun (Korah), a paternal cousin of Sayyiduna Musa among the Children of Israel. Despite knowing the Torah and having once been a scholar, worldly wealth seduced his soul, leading him to ally with Pharaoh and ruthlessly oppress his own beleaguered brethren;
② **«وَاٰتَیْنٰهُ مِنَ الْكُنُوْزِ مَاۤ اِنَّ مَفَاتِحَهٗ لَتَنُوْۤاُ بِالْعُصْبَةِ اُولِی الْقُوَّةِ»** (And We had given him such vast treasures that their very keys were a heavy burden for a band of strong men!) — Classical commentators note that his vaults contained unimaginable mountains of gold, silver, and precious gems, so immense that merely carrying the leather-wrapped keys required an entire brigade of robust, muscular men!
③ **«اِذْ قَالَ لَهٗ قَوْمُهٗ لَا تَفْرَحْ»** (When his righteous people said to him: “Do not boast exultantly;) — Pious believers among the Israelites warned him against intoxicating pride and ostentation;
④ **«اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا یُحِبُّ الْفَرِحِیْنَ»** (“...surely Allah does not love those who boastfully rejoice in worldly pride!”) — Those who become arrogant, ungrateful, and self-satisfied with worldly vanity are despised by their Creator.

① **«وَابْتَغِ فِیمَا آتَاكَ اللَّهُ الدَّارَ الْآخِرَةَ»** (“And seek, through the wealth that Allah has bestowed upon you, the Abode of the Hereafter;”) — The believers outlined the noble Islamic ethos of wealth: utilize your material blessings to earn the pleasure of Allah through charity, relieving the distress of the destitute, and establishing righteousness;
② **«وَلَا تَنْسَ نَصِیْبَكَ مِنَ الدُّنْیَا»** (“...and do not neglect your lawful portion in this world;”) — Islam does not demand total monastic renunciation; enjoy lawful (*halal*) sustenance, decent apparel, and honorable living in moderation;
③ **«وَاَحْسِنْ كَمَاۤ اَحْسَنَ اللّٰهُ اِلَیْكَ»** (“...and do good to others just as Allah has been bountiful and good to you;”) — Reflect divine benevolence by showing kindness, generosity, and compassion to fellow human beings;
④ **«وَلَا تَبْغِ الْفَسَادَ فِی الْاَرْضِ»** (“...and do not seek to spread corruption in the earth;”) — Desist from usury, bribery, tyranny, and supporting oppressors;
⑤ **«اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا یُحِبُّ الْمُفْسِدِیْنَ»** (“...surely Allah does not love the agents of corruption!”) — Sowing social strife and economic exploitation incurs the severe displeasure of Allah.

① **«قَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اُوْتِیْتُهٗ عَلٰی عِلْمٍ عِنْدِیْ»** (He retorted: “I was granted this wealth only because of a specialized knowledge that I possess!”) — Rejecting the pious counsel with wretched narcissism, Qarun attributed his colossal fortune solely to his own financial genius, mercantile cunning, or occult knowledge (alchemy/chemistry), completely denying divine grace;
② **«اَوَلَمْ یَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ قَدْ اَهْلَكَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ»** (Did he not know that Allah had destroyed before him generations...) — A devastating Quranic rebuttal: had worldly wealth and intellect been proof of divine favour, why did Allah obliterate earlier civilizations;
③ **«مَنْ هُوَ اَشَدُّ مِنْهُ قُوَّةً وَّاَكْثَرُ جَمْعًا»** (...who were far mightier than him in physical power and vastly superior in amassed riches?) — The civilizations of 'Ad and Thamud possessed colossal power and treasures dwarfing Qarun's, yet they were crushed into oblivion;
④ **«وَلَا یُسَْٔلُ عَنْ ذُنُوْبِهِمُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ»** (And the criminals will not even be questioned about their sins.) — Their crimes are already comprehensively recorded; they will be dragged straight to Hell without need for inquiry or debate.

① **«فَخَرَجَ عَلٰی قَوْمِهٖ فِیْ زِیْنَتِهٖ»** (So he went forth among his people in all his ostentatious pomp;) — To flaunt his grandeur, Qarun staged a spectacular imperial procession: riding upon a white mule adorned with golden trappings, clothed in purple silk, and flanked by thousands of armed horsemen and liveried servants;
② **«قَالَ الَّذِینَ یُرِیدُونَ الْحَیَاةَ الدُّنْیَا»** (Those who desired merely the worldly life sighed:) — Worldly minded onlookers, seduced by the dazzling spectacle;
③ **«یَا لَیْتَ لَنَا مِثْلَ مَا أُوتِیَ قَارُونُ»** (“Oh, would that we had the like of what Qarun has been granted!”) — Enviously longing for his immense luxury, palaces, and retinue;
④ **«اِنَّهٗ لَذُوْ حَظٍّ عَظِیْمٍ»** (“Indeed, he is a man of tremendous, enviable fortune!”) — Mistakenly identifying temporal affluence with supreme bliss and success.

① **«وَقَالَ الَّذِیْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ وَیْلَكُمْ»** (But those who were endowed with sacred knowledge warned: “Woe to you!) — The God-conscious scholars, blessed with divine insight and discernment, immediately countered the public delusion with righteous indignation;
② **«ثَوَابُ اللّٰهِ خَیْرٌ لِّمَنْ اٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا»** (“The reward of Allah is vastly superior for him who believes and works righteousness;”) — The spiritual ecstasy, forgiveness, and eternal gardens of Paradise promised to the righteous far surpass all the perishable trinkets of Qarun;
③ **«وَلَا یُلَقّٰهَاۤ اِلَّا الصّٰبِرُوْنَ»** (“...and none shall attain this sublime station except the patient and steadfast!”) — Only those who discipline their souls, exercise patience against the temptations of luxury, and remain steadfast in worship are granted this divine wisdom.

① **«فَخَسَفْنَا بِهٖ وَبِدَارِهِ الْاَرْضَ»** (So We caused the earth to swallow him and his palatial mansion!) — When his insolence and hostility towards Sayyiduna Musa peaked, the divine decree was executed: the earth suddenly split open beneath his feet, swallowing Qarun, his towering mansions, his vaults of gold, and his guards down into the subterranean abyss! Classical narrations relate that he continues to sink deeper into the bowels of the earth until the Day of Resurrection;
② **«فَمَا كَانَ لَهٗ مِنْ فِئَةٍ یَّنْصُرُوْنَهٗ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ»** (and he had no faction to help or defend him against Allah,) — Neither his imperial guards, his flattering sycophants, nor his piles of gold could delay the divine punishment by a fraction of a second;
③ **«وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُنْتَصِرِیْنَ»** (nor was he able to save himself or retaliate!) — Completely helpless and destitute in the face of the Almighty’s wrath.

① **«وَاَصْبَحَ الَّذِیْنَ تَمَنَّوْا مَكَانَهٗ بِالْاَمْسِ یَقُوْلُوْنَ»** (And by morning, those who had longed for his position the day before began saying in profound remorse:) — Witnessing the terrifying gaping crater where Qarun’s grand estate had stood, the envious onlookers were struck with shuddering repentance;
② **«وَیْكَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ یَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ یَّشَاۤءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَیَقْدِرُ»** (“Ah! Truly, it is Allah Who expands sustenance for whomever He wills among His servants, and restricts it!”) — Awakening to the spiritual reality: wealth is distributed by divine wisdom as a trial, not as an indicator of divine love;
③ **«لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ مَّنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَیْنَا لَخَسَفَ بِنَا»** (“Had Allah not been gracious to us, He would surely have caused the earth to swallow us as well!”) — Trembling in gratitude that Allah had not answered their foolish prayers for Qarun's fortune;
④ **«وَیْكَاَنَّهٗ لَا یُفْلِحُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ»** (“Ah! Truly, the ungrateful disbelievers shall never prosper!”) — Concluding with absolute certitude that insolence and denial of God culminate in utter ruin.

① **«وَمَا كُنْتَ تَرْجُوْۤا اَنْ یُّلْقٰۤی اِلَیْكَ الْكِتٰبُ»** (And you never anticipated that the Scripture would be revealed unto you...) — Prior to the descent of Archangel Jibril, you neither sought personal grandeur nor worldly office;
② **«اِلَّا رَحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ»** (...except that it came as an exceptional mercy from your Lord;) — Selecting your immaculate soul to receive the ultimate revelation was pure divine grace and cosmic blessing for all existence (*Rahmatan lil-'Alamin*);
③ **«فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ ظَهِیْرًا لِّلْكٰفِرِیْنَ»** (therefore, never be an assistant or supporter to the disbelievers.) — A stern injunction for the Muslim ummah: remain utterly unyielding in faith and never compromise the principles of Islam to appease the desires of idolaters.

① **«وَلَا یَصُدُّنَّكَ عَنْ اٰیٰتِ اللّٰهِ بَعْدَ اِذْ اُنْزِلَتْ اِلَیْكَ»** (And let them never divert you from the verses of Allah after they have been revealed to you;) — Let neither the threats, conspiracies, nor seductive compromises of the Quraysh hinder the recitation and dissemination of divine revelation;
② **«وَادْعُ اِلٰی رَبِّكَ»** (and summon mankind towards your Lord;) — Persist resolutely in calling humanity to the pristine worship of Allah alone;
③ **«وَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِیْنَ»** (and never be among the polytheists.) — Guarding the community from the slightest inclination towards idol-worship or theological compromise.

① **«وَلَا تَدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ»** (And do not invoke any other deity alongside Allah; there is no god worthy of worship except Him!) — The grand climactic declaration of absolute monotheism (*Tawhid*) concluding Surah Al-Qasas;
② **«كُلُّ شَیْءٍ هَالِكٌ اِلَّا وَجْهَهٗ»** (Everything is destined to perish except His Divine Countenance / Entity;) — Classical Sunni exegetes explain that every created entity in the heavens and the earth is fundamentally contingent and transient (*fani*), destined for non-existence, except the Eternal, Self-Subsisting Essence (*Dhat*) of Allah Almighty, and those righteous actions performed solely for His pleasure;
③ **«لَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَاِلَیْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ»** (His alone is the sovereign judgment, and unto Him you shall all be returned!) — The final judicial authority rests with Him alone, and before His majestic tribunal every soul shall be resurrected for eternal recompense. [Thus ends Surah 28: Al-Qasas with complete praise to Allah].
